	)
	(text
		"DESIGN NOTES\n!! MAINS 85-265 VAC on this sheet. All copper left of the HLK-PM01 AC pins is LIVE. !!\nLive path: J1.L -> F1 (T500 mA) -> ACL_F. MOV1 (14D471K) + CX1 (100 nF X2) + RB1 (1M bleeder) across L-N.\nPSU feed: ACL_F -> NTC1 (5D-9 inrush) -> HLK-PM01 AC/L; AC/N -> Neutral. The lamp inrush does NOT pass NTC1.\nHLK-PM01: reinforced-isolation AC-DC, 5 V / 3 W. Its isolation is the primary SELV barrier (>=6 mm creepage).\n5 V rail: CB1 220 uF bulk + C5 100 nF. Feeds the radar (~79 mA, bursty), MCU and opto LED.\nLayout: AC pins and DC pins of PS1 are 29 mm apart - route the isolation slot between them."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "743981f8-902e-58bf-9b84-a6179b6e0f47")
	)
	(text
		"PART NOTES (VERIFY = check against vendor datasheet before release)\nJ1: Lamp returns to Neutral externally. Mark L/N/LAMP on the lid; wire per the install card.\nF1: VERIFY breaking capacity >= prospective fault current; a user-serviceable 5x20 holder is the alt.\nMOV1: VERIFY energy rating for the site; a fused MOV or MOV+GDT improves end-of-life safety.\nRB1: Bleeder: discharges CX1 when unplugged (< 1 s). Rated for continuous 230 Vrms.\nNTC1: Limits turn-on surge into the HLK input cap; the lamp inrush goes through the triac, not here.\nPS1: Reinforced AC-DC isolation is the primary SELV barrier. Keep AC and DC pins' copper apart (slot)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 219.71 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9105c776-4cd3-50db-8683-0910f401de20")
	)
)
